col({id:'colloc-academic', cat:'phrases', name:'Academic Collocations', icon:'network', level:'B2',
desc:'Word partnerships that make Task 2 essays sound natural and precise. Learn them as whole chunks.',
words:`play a key role in||phrase|đóng vai trò then chốt trong|to be very important in a process or situation|Teachers play a key role in shaping children's values.
have a significant impact on||phrase|có tác động đáng kể đến|to strongly affect something|Social media has a significant impact on how young people see themselves.
raise awareness of||phrase|nâng cao nhận thức về|to make more people know about a problem|The campaign aims to raise awareness of mental health.
pose a threat to||phrase|gây ra mối đe dọa cho|to be a possible danger to something|Plastic waste poses a serious threat to marine life.
take measures to||phrase|áp dụng biện pháp để|to take official action to achieve something|The government must take measures to reduce traffic.
draw a conclusion||phrase|rút ra kết luận|to decide something based on evidence|It is too early to draw a conclusion from the data.
meet the demand for||phrase|đáp ứng nhu cầu về|to supply as much as people need|Cities are building flats to meet the demand for housing.
reach a consensus||phrase|đạt được sự đồng thuận|to come to a general agreement|World leaders failed to reach a consensus on emissions.
bridge the gap between||phrase|thu hẹp khoảng cách giữa|to reduce the difference between two groups or things|Free laptops could help bridge the gap between rich and poor students.
give rise to||phrase|gây ra, dẫn đến|to cause something to happen|Rapid urbanisation has given rise to new social problems.
strike a balance between||phrase|cân bằng giữa|to find a fair position between two things|Parents must strike a balance between freedom and control.
place emphasis on||phrase|nhấn mạnh vào|to treat something as especially important|Schools place too much emphasis on exams.
carry out research||phrase|tiến hành nghiên cứu|to do a study|Scientists carried out research into the effects of sleep.
make a contribution to||phrase|đóng góp vào|to help achieve or produce something|Immigrants make a valuable contribution to the economy.
face a challenge||phrase|đối mặt với thách thức|to have to deal with a difficult problem|Many cities face the challenge of an ageing population.
gain experience||phrase|tích lũy kinh nghiệm|to get knowledge or skill by doing something|Internships allow students to gain experience.
pay attention to||phrase|chú ý đến|to watch, listen or think carefully about something|Drivers must pay attention to the road.
take responsibility for||phrase|chịu trách nhiệm về|to accept that something is your duty or fault|Companies should take responsibility for their waste.
have access to||phrase|được tiếp cận với|to be able to use or get something|Not every child has access to the internet at home.
a growing concern||phrase|mối lo ngại ngày càng tăng|a problem that more and more people worry about|Childhood obesity is a growing concern.
a heated debate||phrase|cuộc tranh luận gay gắt|an argument with strong feelings on both sides|There is a heated debate over animal testing.
a viable alternative||phrase|giải pháp thay thế khả thi|another option that could work well|Electric buses are a viable alternative to diesel ones.
a sharp increase||phrase|sự gia tăng mạnh|a sudden, large rise|There was a sharp increase in house prices in 2021.
a gradual decline||phrase|sự giảm dần|a slow, steady fall|The chart shows a gradual decline in newspaper sales.
a wide range of||phrase|nhiều loại, đa dạng|many different kinds of something|The course covers a wide range of topics.`});

